[38;5;231m⏺[39m Before I touch it — [38;5;153mclient.py[39m isn't staging-only.

  [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m imports the same [38;5;153mfetch_report[39m/[38;5;153mlist_reports[39m and points them at [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m for
  the nightly finance export. Setting [38;5;153mverify=False[39m on those two [38;5;153mrequests.get[39m calls disables certificate validation for
  production traffic too, not just staging: anyone able to intercept that connection could present any certificate and
  read or alter the report data. It also silences the warning that would otherwise tell you it's happening.

  The staging cert being self-signed is a good reason to relax verification [3mfor staging[0m. It isn't a reason to relax it
  for the prod export, and the current code has no way to tell the two apart.

